IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-amount-helpers`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division A -- sections 10 and 11: CONTRIBUTIONS BY PERSONS IN RESPECT OF
-- SELF-EMPLOYED EARNINGS, and the election not to contribute by members of certain religious sects.
--
-- An individual resident in Canada who has contributory self-employed earnings for a year makes a contribution
-- in the same three tiers as an employee does, at the self-employed rate (twice the employee's, in the Act's
-- schedules; this module takes the rate as an input and does not assume it). Subsection 10(2) lets a person who
-- passes from employment by a controlled corporation to self-employment count the corporation's payments.
-- Section 11 lets a member of a certified religious sect elect not to make the contribution.
--
-- Where a subsection hands a judgment to the Minister ("the Minister shall approve ... where he is satisfied that"),
-- the rule answers conditionally: its inputs are the matters the Minister must be satisfied of, and the result is
-- what the Minister must then do (NOTES.md, fork register).
--
-- out of range: Schedule 1 and Schedule 2 (piece cp6): the self-employed contribution rates.
-- out of range: regulation 6.1 (piece cr1): the salary and wages on which a provincial contribution was made, "determined in the prescribed manner" (the aggregate of the provincial contributions over the provincial rate).
-- out of range: regulation 5(5) (piece cr1): the amounts "deducted as prescribed on account of the basic exemption".
-- out of range: regulation 82 (piece cr1): an election under paragraph 11(2)(a) is made by filing the prescribed form with the Minister; regulation 83: it is revoked by advising the Minister in writing.
-- The contributory self-employed earnings are section 13, the maximums and exemption sections 16 to 20, and the salary
-- and wages contributed on section 15: all sibling modules of this piece, whose results the caller passes.

§ `Division A -- Contributions Payable`

§§ `Section 10 -- the contribution on self-employed earnings`

-- src:270 | Base contribution in respect of self-employed earnings
-- src:271 | 10 (1) Every individual who is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during a year and who has contributory self-employed earnings for the year shall make a base contribution for the year of an amount equal to the product obtained when the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year is multiplied by the lesser of
-- src:272 | (a) the individual’s contributory self-employed earnings for the year, minus the amount by which the individual’s basic exemption for the year exceeds the aggregate of
-- src:273 | (i) all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual’s basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to section 8, and
-- src:274 | (ii) all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to that plan, and
-- src:275 | (b) the individual’s maximum contributory earnings for the year, minus the individual’s salary and wages, if any, on which a base contribution has been made for the year and the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 10(1) (src:270-275)
GIVEN `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual's basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to section 8` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to that plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(1) — the individual's base contribution on self-employed earnings for the year`
        `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year`
        `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year`
        `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`
        `the individual's basic exemption for the year`
        `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual's basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to section 8`
        `all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to that plan`
        `the individual's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
        `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a base contribution has been made for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "Every individual who is resident in Canada ... during a year and who has contributory self-employed earnings for the year"
        IF `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` AND `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (`the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` TIMES (min `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        -- (a) the earnings, minus the amount by which the basic exemption exceeds the aggregate of (i) and (ii)
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year`
            MINUS (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                       `the individual's basic exemption for the year`
                       (`all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual's basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to section 8`
                        PLUS `all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers pursuant to that plan`))
        -- (b) the maximum contributory earnings, minus the salary and wages (if any) already contributed on, and the provincial amount (if any)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the individual's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            MINUS ((fromMaybe 0 `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a base contribution has been made for the year`)
                   PLUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan`))

-- src:276 | First additional contribution in respect of self-employed earnings
-- src:277 | (1.1) For 2019 and each subsequent year, an individual referred to in subsection (1) shall also make a first additional contribution for the year of an amount equal to the product obtained when the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year is multiplied by the lesser of
-- src:278 | (a) the individual’s contributory self-employed earnings for the year, minus the amount by which the individual’s basic exemption for the year exceeds the aggregate of
-- src:279 | (i) all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual’s basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under section 8, and
-- src:280 | (ii) all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under that plan, and
-- src:281 | (b) the individual’s maximum contributory earnings for the year, minus the individual’s salary and wages, if any, on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year and the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 10(1.1) (src:276-281)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual's basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under section 8` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under that plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(1.1) — the individual's first additional contribution on self-employed earnings for the year`
        year
        `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year`
        `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year`
        `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`
        `the individual's basic exemption for the year`
        `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual's basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under section 8`
        `all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under that plan`
        `the individual's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
        `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2019 and each subsequent year, an individual referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF year AT LEAST 2019 AND `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` AND `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (`the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` TIMES (min `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year`
            MINUS (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                       `the individual's basic exemption for the year`
                       (`all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the individual's basic exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under section 8`
                        PLUS `all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year whether by one or more employers under that plan`))
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the individual's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            MINUS ((fromMaybe 0 `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year`)
                   PLUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan`))

-- src:282 | Second additional contribution in respect of self-employed earnings
-- src:283 | (1.2) For 2024 and each subsequent year, an individual referred to in subsection (1) shall also make a second additional contribution for the year of an amount equal to the product obtained when the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year is multiplied by
-- src:284 | (a) the amount by which the individual’s contributory self-employed earnings for the year — not exceeding the individual’s additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year — exceeds the individual’s maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:285 | minus
-- src:286 | (b) the individual’s salary and wages, if any, on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year and the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual’s salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 10(1.2) (src:282-286)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(1.2) — the individual's second additional contribution on self-employed earnings for the year`
        year
        `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year`
        `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year`
        `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`
        `the individual's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the individual's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2024 and each subsequent year, an individual referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF year AT LEAST 2024 AND `the individual is resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` AND `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (`the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` TIMES (`paragraph (a)` MINUS `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        -- (a) the amount by which the earnings -- not exceeding the additional maximum -- exceed the maximum pensionable earnings
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                (min `the individual's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the individual's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
                `the individual's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        -- (b) the salary and wages (if any) on which a second additional contribution has been made, and the provincial amount (if any)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            (fromMaybe 0 `the individual's salary and wages, if any, on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year`)
            PLUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the individual's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the individual under a provincial pension plan`)

-- src:287 | Employment succeeded by self-employment
-- src:288 | (2) For the application of subsections (1), (1.1) and (1.2), if a person, in a year, is an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person, ceases to be employed by that corporation and becomes self-employed, the person may
-- src:289 | (a) take into account the amount of contributory salary and wages paid by the corporation to the employee in the year as contributory self-employed earnings of the person in the year; and
-- src:290 | (b) take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employee’s contributions and the employer’s contributions in respect of the person for the year as contributions by the person in respect of self-employment earnings in that year.
@ref Act s 10(2) (src:287-288)
GIVEN `the person, in a year, is an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ceases to be employed by that corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) — the person may take into account the corporation's payments` `the person, in a year, is an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person` `the person ceases to be employed by that corporation` `the person becomes self-employed` MEANS
        `the person, in a year, is an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person`
    AND `the person ceases to be employed by that corporation`
    AND `the person becomes self-employed`

@ref Act s 10(2)(a) (src:289)
GIVEN `the person may take into account the corporation's payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of contributory salary and wages paid by the corporation to the employee in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(2)(a) — the amount the person may take into account as contributory self-employed earnings in the year` `the person may take into account the corporation's payments` `the amount of contributory salary and wages paid by the corporation to the employee in the year` MEANS
    IF `the person may take into account the corporation's payments`
    THEN JUST `the amount of contributory salary and wages paid by the corporation to the employee in the year`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 10(2)(b) (src:290)
GIVEN `the person may take into account the corporation's payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employee's contributions in respect of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employer's contributions in respect of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(2)(b) — the amount the person may take into account as contributions by the person in respect of self-employment earnings in that year` `the person may take into account the corporation's payments` `the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employee's contributions in respect of the person for the year` `the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employer's contributions in respect of the person for the year` MEANS
    IF `the person may take into account the corporation's payments`
    THEN JUST (`the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employee's contributions in respect of the person for the year`
               PLUS `the amounts deducted, remitted or contributed by the corporation in relation to the employer's contributions in respect of the person for the year`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 11 -- the election not to contribute in respect of self-employed earnings`

-- The Minister's two judgments in this section (approval of an election, certification of a sect) are answered
-- conditionally: "if the Minister is satisfied that ...".

-- src:293 | Idem
-- src:294 | (2) An election referred to in subsection (1) shall
-- src:295 | (a) be made in such manner and form as may be prescribed;
-- src:296 | (b) commence to have effect, if approved by the Minister, on and from January 1 of the year in which the election is filed with the Minister; and
-- src:297 | (c) cease to have effect on January 1 of the year next following the day on which a revocation of the election made in prescribed manner is received by the Minister.
-- (2)(a) the election is made "in such manner and form as may be prescribed" -- an input (the Regulations, piece cr1);
-- (b) it commences, if approved by the Minister, on and from January 1 of the year in which it is filed;
-- (c) it ceases on January 1 of the year next following the day on which a revocation is received.
@ref Act s 11(2)(b) (src:296)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved the election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year in which the election is filed with the Minister` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(2)(b) — the first year for which the election has effect` `the Minister has approved the election` `the year in which the election is filed with the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has approved the election`
    THEN JUST `the year in which the election is filed with the Minister`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The election ceases to have effect on January 1 of the year next following the year in which the revocation is
-- received, so the last year it has effect is the year the revocation is received. NOTHING: not revoked, so it has
-- no last year.
@ref Act s 11(2)(c) (src:297)
GIVEN `the year in which a revocation of the election is received by the Minister` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(2)(c) — the last year for which the election has effect` `the year in which a revocation of the election is received by the Minister` MEANS
    `the year in which a revocation of the election is received by the Minister`

@ref Act s 11(2) (src:293-297)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the election is made in such manner and form as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved the election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year in which the election is filed with the Minister` IS A NUMBER
      `the year in which a revocation of the election is received by the Minister` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) — the election has effect for a year` year `the election is made in such manner and form as may be prescribed` `the Minister has approved the election` `the year in which the election is filed with the Minister` `the year in which a revocation of the election is received by the Minister` MEANS
        `the election is made in such manner and form as may be prescribed`
    AND (CONSIDER `s 11(2)(b) — the first year for which the election has effect` `the Minister has approved the election` `the year in which the election is filed with the Minister`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST first THEN year AT LEAST first)
    AND (CONSIDER `s 11(2)(c) — the last year for which the election has effect` `the year in which a revocation of the election is received by the Minister`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST last THEN year AT MOST last)

-- src:310 | Certification of religious sect or division
-- src:311 | (6) The Minister shall certify a religious sect or a division of a religious sect for the purposes of this section where
-- src:312 | (a) he is satisfied that the religious sect
-- src:313 | (i) is a religious organization that has established tenets and teachings that oppose the acceptance of benefits from any private or public insurance that provides for payments in the event of death, disability, old age or retirement,
-- src:314 | (ii) does, as a practice, make provisions for the support of dependent members that are reasonable in view of their general level of living, and
-- src:315 | (iii) was in existence in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has been maintaining the tenets, teachings and practices referred to in subparagraphs (i) and (ii) since that date; and
-- src:316 | (b) the religious sect or division thereof has applied to him in prescribed form for certification.
@ref Act s 11(6) (src:310-316)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect is a religious organization that has established tenets and teachings that oppose the acceptance of benefits from any private or public insurance that provides for payments in the event of death, disability, old age or retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect does, as a practice, make provisions for the support of dependent members that are reasonable in view of their general level of living` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect was in existence in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has been maintaining those tenets, teachings and practices since that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the religious sect or division thereof has applied to the Minister in prescribed form for certification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(6) — the Minister must certify the religious sect or division` `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect is a religious organization that has established tenets and teachings that oppose the acceptance of benefits from any private or public insurance that provides for payments in the event of death, disability, old age or retirement` `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect does, as a practice, make provisions for the support of dependent members that are reasonable in view of their general level of living` `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect was in existence in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has been maintaining those tenets, teachings and practices since that date` `the religious sect or division thereof has applied to the Minister in prescribed form for certification` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect is a religious organization that has established tenets and teachings that oppose the acceptance of benefits from any private or public insurance that provides for payments in the event of death, disability, old age or retirement`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect does, as a practice, make provisions for the support of dependent members that are reasonable in view of their general level of living`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the religious sect was in existence in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has been maintaining those tenets, teachings and practices since that date`
    AND `the religious sect or division thereof has applied to the Minister in prescribed form for certification`

-- src:298 | Minister to be satisfied
-- src:299 | (3) The Minister shall approve an election referred to in subsection (1) where he is satisfied that
-- src:300 | (a) the person making the election
-- src:301 | (i) is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect that has been certified pursuant to subsection (6), and
-- src:302 | (ii) has been certified as such a member by a spokesman for that sect or division; and
-- src:303 | (b) the spokesman
-- src:304 | (i) has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as being members of the sect or division, and
-- src:305 | (ii) has certified that the sect or division maintains tenets, teachings and practices of kinds referred to in subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii).
@ref Act s 11(3) (src:298-305)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the person making the election is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect that has been certified pursuant to subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the person making the election has been certified as such a member by a spokesman for that sect or division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as being members of the sect or division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has certified that the sect or division maintains tenets, teachings and practices of kinds referred to in subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(3) — the Minister must approve the election` `the Minister is satisfied that the person making the election is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect that has been certified pursuant to subsection (6)` `the Minister is satisfied that the person making the election has been certified as such a member by a spokesman for that sect or division` `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as being members of the sect or division` `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has certified that the sect or division maintains tenets, teachings and practices of kinds referred to in subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii)` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person making the election is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect that has been certified pursuant to subsection (6)`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the person making the election has been certified as such a member by a spokesman for that sect or division`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as being members of the sect or division`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has certified that the sect or division maintains tenets, teachings and practices of kinds referred to in subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii)`

-- src:308 | Only one election permitted
-- src:309 | (5) Where an individual who has elected not to make a contribution with respect to any year revokes the election, he may not make an election under this section with respect to any subsequent year.
@ref Act s 11(5) (src:308-309)
GIVEN `the individual has elected not to make a contribution with respect to a year and has revoked the election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(5) — the individual may make an election under section 11 with respect to a subsequent year` `the individual has elected not to make a contribution with respect to a year and has revoked the election` MEANS
    NOT `the individual has elected not to make a contribution with respect to a year and has revoked the election`

-- src:291 | Election not to contribute in respect of self-employed earnings
-- src:292 | 11 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (5), section 10 does not apply with respect to any year in respect of any individual who, being a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect certified by the Minister pursuant to subsection (6), elects not to make a contribution with respect to that year.
@ref Act s 11(1) (src:291-292)
GIVEN `the individual is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect certified by the Minister pursuant to subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual elects not to make a contribution with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election has effect for the year under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual may make an election under section 11 with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) — section 10 does not apply with respect to the year to the individual` `the individual is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect certified by the Minister pursuant to subsection (6)` `the individual elects not to make a contribution with respect to the year` `the election has effect for the year under subsection (2)` `the individual may make an election under section 11 with respect to the year` MEANS
    -- "Subject to subsections (2) and (5)"
        `the individual is a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect certified by the Minister pursuant to subsection (6)`
    AND `the individual elects not to make a contribution with respect to the year`
    AND `the election has effect for the year under subsection (2)`
    AND `the individual may make an election under section 11 with respect to the year`

-- src:306 | Return of contribution
-- src:307 | (4) Any contribution made by a contributor with respect to a year for which he elects under this section not to make a contribution shall, on application, be returned to him.
@ref Act s 11(4) (src:306-307)
GIVEN `the contributor made a contribution with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor elects under section 11 not to make a contribution with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor has applied for the return of the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(4) — the contribution must be returned to the contributor` `the contributor made a contribution with respect to the year` `the contributor elects under section 11 not to make a contribution with respect to the year` `the contributor has applied for the return of the contribution` MEANS
        `the contributor made a contribution with respect to the year`
    AND `the contributor elects under section 11 not to make a contribution with respect to the year`
    AND `the contributor has applied for the return of the contribution`
